{"explanation":"Migrate EncryptedKey encryption to an explicitly prepared AES-GCM cipher with a fresh 96-bit nonce and a versioned current-record marker. New records retain the Cipher-generated encoded parameters; legacy records retain their existing parameter decoding path. Package-private accessors allow the coordinated production callers to select the current versus legacy wrapping-key lifecycle and allow target-focused tests to inspect retained parameters without reflection.","review_assumptions":["Android's supported AES/GCM provider exposes AlgorithmParameters under the standard "GCM" algorithm name when AES/GCM/NoPadding is available.","The existing record serializer/deserializer leaves a newly added absent integer field at Java's default value of zero, so persisted records produced before this change are interpreted as legacy version 0.","Coordinated Encryptor and MasterKey edits will only pass lifecycle-approved wrapping keys to prepareEncryptionCipher/encrypt(Cipher, SecretKey), and will use usesCurrentWrappingKey() before choosing a wrapping-key lifecycle for decryption."],"no_change_required":false,"decision":"MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW","confidence":"medium","edits":[{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/EncryptedKey.java","original_code":"package org.fedorahosted.freeotp.encryptor;

import android.util.Log;

import java.io.IOException;
import java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets;
import java.security.AlgorithmParameters;
import java.security.InvalidAlgorithmParameterException;
import java.security.InvalidKeyException;
import java.security.NoSuchAlgorithmException;

import javax.crypto.BadPaddingException;
import javax.crypto.Cipher;
import javax.crypto.IllegalBlockSizeException;
import javax.crypto.NoSuchPaddingException;
import javax.crypto.SecretKey;
import javax.crypto.spec.SecretKeySpec;

public final class EncryptedKey {
    private final byte[] mCipherText;
    private final byte[] mParameters;
    private final String mCipher;
    private final String mToken;

    private EncryptedKey(Cipher cipher, SecretKey token)
            throws BadPaddingException, IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException {
        mCipher = cipher.getAlgorithm();
        mToken = token.getAlgorithm();

        cipher.updateAAD(mToken.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
        mCipherText = cipher.doFinal(token.getEncoded());
        mParameters = cipher.getParameters().getEncoded();
    }

    public static EncryptedKey encrypt(SecretKey key, SecretKey plaintext)
            throws NoSuchAlgorithmException, NoSuchPaddingException, InvalidKeyException,
            BadPaddingException, IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException {
        if (key == null) {
            throw new InvalidKeyException("Key is null");
        }
        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance("AES/GCM/NoPadding");
        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, key);
        return new EncryptedKey(cipher, plaintext);
    }

    public SecretKey decrypt(SecretKey key)
            throws NoSuchPaddingException, NoSuchAlgorithmException, BadPaddingException,
            IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException, InvalidAlgorithmParameterException,
            InvalidKeyException {
        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance(mCipher);
        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, key);
        String algorithm = cipher.getParameters().getAlgorithm();

        AlgorithmParameters ap = AlgorithmParameters.getInstance(algorithm);
        ap.init(mParameters);

        cipher.init(Cipher.DECRYPT_MODE, key, ap);
        cipher.updateAAD(mToken.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
        return new SecretKeySpec(cipher.doFinal(mCipherText), mToken);
    }
}
","edit_kind":"declaration","corrected_code":"package org.fedorahosted.freeotp.encryptor;

import android.util.Log;

import java.io.IOException;
import java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets;
import java.security.AlgorithmParameters;
import java.security.InvalidAlgorithmParameterException;
import java.security.InvalidKeyException;
import java.security.NoSuchAlgorithmException;
import java.security.SecureRandom;

import javax.crypto.BadPaddingException;
import javax.crypto.Cipher;
import javax.crypto.IllegalBlockSizeException;
import javax.crypto.NoSuchPaddingException;
import javax.crypto.SecretKey;
import javax.crypto.spec.GCMParameterSpec;
import javax.crypto.spec.SecretKeySpec;

public final class EncryptedKey {
    private static final String GCM_TRANSFORMATION = "AES/GCM/NoPadding";
    private static final String GCM_PARAMETERS_ALGORITHM = "GCM";
    private static final int GCM_TAG_LENGTH_BITS = 128;
    private static final int GCM_NONCE_LENGTH_BYTES = 12;
    private static final int LEGACY_RECORD_VERSION = 0;
    private static final int CURRENT_RECORD_VERSION = 1;
    private static final SecureRandom SECURE_RANDOM = new SecureRandom();

    private final byte[] mCipherText;
    private final byte[] mParameters;
    private final String mCipher;
    private final String mToken;
    private final int mVersion;

    private EncryptedKey(Cipher cipher, SecretKey token)
            throws BadPaddingException, IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException {
        mCipher = cipher.getAlgorithm();
        mToken = token.getAlgorithm();
        mVersion = CURRENT_RECORD_VERSION;

        cipher.updateAAD(mToken.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
        mCipherText = cipher.doFinal(token.getEncoded());
        mParameters = cipher.getParameters().getEncoded();
    }

    /**
     * Prepares the current record format's AES-GCM encryption cipher for a wrapping key selected
     * by the caller's approved key lifecycle.
     */
    static Cipher prepareEncryptionCipher(SecretKey key)
            throws NoSuchAlgorithmException, NoSuchPaddingException, InvalidKeyException,
            InvalidAlgorithmParameterException {
        if (key == null) {
            throw new InvalidKeyException("Key is null");
        }

        byte[] nonce = new byte[GCM_NONCE_LENGTH_BYTES];
        SECURE_RANDOM.nextBytes(nonce);

        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance(GCM_TRANSFORMATION);
        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, key,
                new GCMParameterSpec(GCM_TAG_LENGTH_BITS, nonce));
        return cipher;
    }

    /**
     * Retained public entry point for callers that have not yet prepared a lifecycle cipher.
     */
    public static EncryptedKey encrypt(SecretKey key, SecretKey plaintext)
            throws NoSuchAlgorithmException, NoSuchPaddingException, InvalidKeyException,
            BadPaddingException, IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException,
            InvalidAlgorithmParameterException {
        return encrypt(prepareEncryptionCipher(key), plaintext);
    }

    /**
     * Stores a token using a cipher prepared by the caller's approved wrapping-key lifecycle.
     */
    static EncryptedKey encrypt(Cipher cipher, SecretKey plaintext)
            throws BadPaddingException, IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException, InvalidKeyException {
        if (cipher == null) {
            throw new InvalidKeyException("Cipher is null");
        }
        return new EncryptedKey(cipher, plaintext);
    }

    /**
     * Identifies records whose wrapping key must be resolved through the current lifecycle.
     */
    boolean usesCurrentWrappingKey() {
        return mVersion == CURRENT_RECORD_VERSION;
    }

    /**
     * Returns a defensive copy of the retained Cipher parameters for internal compatibility tests.
     */
    byte[] getEncodedParameters() {
        return (byte[]) mParameters.clone();
    }

    public SecretKey decrypt(SecretKey key)
            throws NoSuchPaddingException, NoSuchAlgorithmException, BadPaddingException,
            IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException, InvalidAlgorithmParameterException,
            InvalidKeyException {
        if (mVersion != LEGACY_RECORD_VERSION && mVersion != CURRENT_RECORD_VERSION) {
            throw new IOException("Unsupported encrypted key record version: " + mVersion);
        }

        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance(mCipher);
        AlgorithmParameters parameters = AlgorithmParameters.getInstance(GCM_PARAMETERS_ALGORITHM);
        parameters.init(mParameters);

        cipher.init(Cipher.DECRYPT_MODE, key, parameters);
        cipher.updateAAD(mToken.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
        return new SecretKeySpec(cipher.doFinal(mCipherText), mToken);
    }
}
","reason":"Use an explicit fresh AES-GCM nonce and GCMParameterSpec for all newly written records, retain the Cipher-generated encoded parameters, and mark current records so coordinated callers can preserve legacy wrapping-key resolution for version-0 persisted records. The decryption path continues to consume the stored transformation, AAD algorithm identifier, and encoded GCM parameters without performing an unnecessary encryption initialization." ,"symbol":"EncryptedKey"}],"manual_review_required":true,"provided_contracts":["Package-private Cipher prepareEncryptionCipher(SecretKey) prepares AES/GCM/NoPadding with a fresh 96-bit nonce and 128-bit tag for a caller-provided approved wrapping key.","Package-private EncryptedKey encrypt(Cipher, SecretKey) accepts a caller-prepared current-lifecycle cipher; public encrypt(SecretKey, SecretKey) remains available and uses the same current preparation path.","Package-private boolean usesCurrentWrappingKey() returns false for persisted legacy records whose added version field is absent/default zero and true for newly created version-1 records.","Package-private byte[] getEncodedParameters() returns a defensive copy of retained parameters for non-reflective package-level regression tests.","decrypt(SecretKey) retains the existing public signature and decrypts stored AES-GCM records using their retained transformation, AAD algorithm identifier, and encoded parameters."],"required_contracts":["Encryptor and MasterKey must resolve current versus legacy wrapping keys before decryption using EncryptedKey.usesCurrentWrappingKey().","Encryptor and MasterKey must create current records by obtaining their approved wrapping key, calling EncryptedKey.prepareEncryptionCipher(key), and passing that cipher to EncryptedKey.encrypt(cipher, plaintext).","The dedicated EncryptedKey instrumentation test must decode getEncodedParameters() as GCM AlgorithmParameters/GCMParameterSpec and compare nonce bytes rather than comparing separately constructed parameter objects."],"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/EncryptedKey.java","required_tests":["Round-trip current records through both coordinated AndroidKeyStore-backed Encryptor and PBKDF2-backed MasterKey lifecycles.","Encrypt repeatedly with one approved wrapping key; assert decoded retained GCM nonces differ and every record decrypts.","Decrypt representative version-0 records through the coordinated legacy AndroidKeyStore and PBKDF2 wrapping-key paths using their retained encoded parameters."]}
